%% Document ingestion + indexing pipeline
%% Key points: connectors do crawl-then-sync; ACLs captured at ingestion;
%% ACL sync runs on a separate faster loop than content sync.

flowchart TB
    subgraph Sources["Customer source systems"]
        SP[SharePoint]
        GD[Google Drive]
        CF[Confluence]
        SL[Slack]
    end

    CONN[Connectors<br/>initial crawl → incremental sync<br/>change events, polling fallback]

    Q{{Work queue<br/>per-tenant fairness<br/>incremental prioritised over backfill}}

    subgraph Pipeline["Processing pipeline — idempotent per doc_id + content_hash"]
        direction TB
        P1[1 · Fetch bytes]
        P2[2 · Dedupe by content hash]
        P3[3 · Parse<br/>PDF/Office/HTML → text + structure<br/>OCR if scanned · Transcribe if audio]
        P4[4 · Chunk<br/>structure-aware ~500 tokens, 15% overlap<br/>keep tables and code intact]
        P5[5 · Capture ACL from source<br/>stamp allowed_principals + acl_version]
        P6[6 · Embed — batched on GPU]
        P7[7 · Upsert to indexes]
        P1 --> P2 --> P3 --> P4 --> P5 --> P6 --> P7
    end

    VS[(Vector store)]
    BM[(BM25 index)]
    META[(Metadata DB<br/>doc status, versions)]
    DLQ[(Dead letter queue<br/>parse failures, surfaced to customer)]

    ACLSYNC[ACL sync loop<br/>runs more frequently than content sync<br/>permissions change fast and matter more]

    Sources --> CONN --> Q --> Pipeline
    P7 --> VS
    P7 --> BM
    P7 --> META
    Pipeline -.failures.-> DLQ
    Sources --> ACLSYNC --> VS
